---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Riviera Events"
  description="Local events for Azizi Riviera residents — what's actually on in the development, not a citywide events calendar."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Events</p>
    <h1>What's on, locally</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Community meetups, promenade openings, and seasonal happenings
      specific to Riviera — kept separate from <a href="/news/">news</a>
      because "what's on this week" and "what's changed in the
      development" are different questions with different shelf lives.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What counts as a local event here</h2>
    <p>
      Anything organized in or around Riviera specifically — resident
      meetups, promenade tenant launches, seasonal activity on the canal
      walkway. Citywide festivals and events get plenty of coverage
      elsewhere; this page deliberately doesn't duplicate that.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Follow along</h2>
    <p>
      The fastest-moving version of this lives on Instagram
      (<strong>@rivieradst</strong>) rather than here — this page is the
      durable, searchable record, while the Instagram account is where it
      happens first.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

